<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

<!--
    MoEventsChancesZeroed_RuledCut.xml                          Jawa_Patches
    ============================================================================
    MODLIST_RULED_CUTS_1, owner ruling (bench sitting 2026-09-12): zero every
    `MO_*` IncidentDef's `baseChance` from Mo'Events (Continued) — the mod
    itself STAYS active (its ThingDefs/JobDefs/other content are not being
    touched) until `RUT_SCAVENGEREVENTS_BUILD_1`'s own port of this content
    lands; until then its incidents simply never fire.

    🔴 A naive `grep '<defName>'` on the donor's file finds THIRTEEN `MO_`
    defNames, and that count is wrong. Three of them —
    `MO_Recovery` ("Not working correctly right now"), `MO_Calm` ("Bugged"),
    `MO_GoodRest` ("Not working like I want to right now") — sit entirely
    inside the donor's OWN XML comment blocks in
    `Defs/IncidentDef/IncidentDefs.xml`; they never load, so a
    `PatchOperationReplace` targeting them would match nothing and log
    nothing (this project's own repeated lesson: a patch that matches
    nothing logs nothing — verified here by parsing the file with
    `xml.etree.ElementTree`, which correctly skips comments, rather than
    trusting the grep count). Confirmed with `python3
    xml.etree.ElementTree.parse` before writing this patch, not guessed.

    The TEN real, live defNames and their shipped `baseChance` (2026-09-13
    capture): MO_Stroke(1.5) MO_SurvivalPod(1.5) MO_Nausea(3) MO_Insects(1.5)
    MO_PodCrash(2) MO_Thanksgiving(2) MO_ShipBreak(1) MO_Amnesia(2)
    MO_RescueTraitor(2) MO_Migration(5) — every live `IncidentDef` in the
    donor's file uses the `MO_` prefix, so `PatchOperationReplace` on these
    ten covers every incident the mod can actually fire.

    ⚠️ Not done via the mod's own in-game settings window: `rimworld/
    get_mod_settings` on its settings surface (`mod-settings:mlie.moevents:*`)
    returned an EMPTY object (`topLevelSettingCount: 0`) — this mod's settings
    class exposes nothing to generic reflection, and no `Mod_2035143365_*.xml`
    settings file has ever been written to `Config/` (checked — none exists),
    so there is nothing a runtime settings write could reach either. Patching
    `baseChance` directly at the def is the mechanism this mod's own
    `IncidentWorker` actually reads from, and it survives a cold load without
    depending on a settings file existing.
-->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Mo'Events (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_Stroke"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_SurvivalPod"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_Nausea"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_Insects"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_PodCrash"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_Thanksgiving"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_ShipBreak"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_Amnesia"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_RescueTraitor"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="MO_Migration"]/baseChance</xpath>
          <value><baseChance>0</baseChance></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
